  "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/BBTTCC%20Button%20Icons/BBTTCC_button_icon_asteroid.png",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Normalized Ancestry Feat.</strong> Formerly granted automatically by <em>Oldenborn (Earthbound)</em> at level 17; now available as an optional ancestry feat.</p><p><em>“Reality tries to slide. You say: no.”</em></p>\n        <p><strong>World-Anchor (1/Long Rest).</strong> When you or an ally you can see within 30 feet would be teleported, displaced, banished, or forcibly moved by a magical or metaphysical effect, you can use your reaction to anchor them. The effect fails, and the attacker takes psychic backlash equal to your proficiency bonus.</p>\n        <p><strong>BBTTCC Hook.</strong> In strategic play, your faction treats Slippage in your current hex as one step less severe for 1 Turn (handled by BBTTCC flags / GM).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
